ll,"pacing":"60","max_frame_stall_ms":64.072},"checksum":"2643caa3","notes":"Flutter Dart-AOT release, Linux GTK3 embedder, renderer: Impeller (OpenGL ES backend, default), GL = Mesa (llvmpipe under Xvfb). frame_ms = interval between consecutive FrameTiming rasterFinish timestamps (SchedulerBinding.addTimingsCallback; raster thread finished the frame and handed it to the GTK GL compositor; latest public post-render signal, not an X11 present timestamp). Only frames the engine rasterized are counted (Flutter produces no frame when nothing is dirty; every animated frame changes content). Pacing (BENCH_PACING, requested=60): native Flutter cadence = Ticker/SchedulerBinding frames driven by the engine vsync; the Linux GTK embedder registers no vsync callback, so the engine uses its fallback vsync waiter with a fixed 1/60 s tick (engine source shell/common/vsync_waiter_fallback.cc). No public/documented API uncaps it, so uncapped -> pacing \"60-only\". gc = null: Dart exposes no GC counters in AOT release. Warm-up 2 s; script time frozen at 0 during warm-up. canvas: every shape (own 2-colour linear gradient, and for 1 in 10 its MaskFilter.blur(sigma 4) shadow at offset (2,2)) is recorded once into a sprite atlas (PictureRecorder + Picture.toImageSync, 8 page(s) 512 px wide, 3681 px total height, sprites assigned to pages in index order); each frame = one Canvas.drawRawAtlas per page, pages in order = shapes in z-order (translation-only RSTransforms, bilinear sampling) inside clipRRect 1000x600 r16; graph drawRawPoints(polygon) 10000 pts stroke 1 px rebuilt per frame.","unsupported":null}